 going to do the most  damage in the letter to sponsors the  group wrote the consequence of mr  goodell's decisions around the  investigation and the lack of any  meaningful action against dan snyder is  to tell women and survivors everywhere  you and your experiences do not matter  to the nfl it is the first instance i  can recall in which there was not a  written report amy trask was the first  female ceo in the league and is now an  nfl analyst for cbs sports going to  sponsors and trying to apply pressure  is that a  smart way to try to incentivize the nfl  or force the nfl's hand it's a tried and  true  method so i'm not surprised that they're  doing it but i don't know if it will  work for applegate the fight extends  beyond the nfl this isn't just a sports  issue this is an issue throughout any  industry in order for us to make a great  change why not  start with one of the most recognized  organizations in the world  we reached out to the six major nfl  sponsors mentioned in that letter who  was sent that letter but have not heard  back the group applegate is working with  may not be alone in their fight though  the nfl players association has said it  plans to petition the nfl and call for  the release of all the emails associated  with the investigation and amy trask and  i discussed this idea of transparency  and why not say  this is who we were  we're working on getting better show  everybody what's there obviously there  are a lot of issues and there are other  things we may or may not know but all we  can do is speculate unless a formal  written report is released is there any  indica was there any question all the  emails come out the nfl so far has said  that they are not releasing any of this  information but the nfl players  association once they start negotiating  their collective bargaining agreement  could have some sway if they do try to  hold out to get these emails released  and see what else is in there it is  larger  than just the nfl we've seen this over  and over again when bad behavior is  investigated sometimes the results of  those investigations are not made public  they need to be  transparency
 

